WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.732
Grain remains the central safety rule.

00:00:02.732 --> 00:00:07.577
A common table expression can have a different grain from the source table.

00:00:07.577 --> 00:00:11.857
A window function usually preserves the current row grain.

00:00:11.857 --> 00:00:17.752
A later filter can reduce the number of rows without changing what one row represents.

00:00:17.752 --> 00:00:24.959
If you cannot explain the row meaning at each stage, advanced syntax can hide mistakes instead of solving them.
